<Layout home title="KabuForge — Japanese Equity Research and Backtesting" description="Open-source local-first Japanese equity research: J-Quants or explicit local data, factor and ML research, backtesting, portfolio construction, risk controls and Japanese broker-neutral planning."><p class="eyebrow">OPEN SOURCE · LOCAL FIRST · JAPANESE EQUITIES</p><div class="hero"><div><h1>Reproducible research.<br/>Japanese equities.</h1><p class="lead">J-Quants or your explicitly selected local data → Factor + ML → Backtest → Portfolio → Risk → Japanese broker planning. Keep every research input local and inspectable.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/docs/quickstart/">Get started</a><a class="secondary" href="https://github.com/Siyuan-chat/KabuForge">View on GitHub</a></div><p class="version">0.1.1 · tag v0.1.1 · Python 3.12+ · AGPL-3.0-only</p><p class="candidate-version">Main source candidate {versionInfo.version} · {versionInfo.release_status} (unpublished)</p></div><div class="architecture-card"><div class="card-label">DECISION PIPELINE</div><ol><li><b>01</b> J-Quants / local data <small>User-selected inputs</small></li><li><b>02</b> Factor + ML <small>Research features and models</small></li><li><b>03</b> Backtest <small>Declared execution assumptions</small></li><li><b>04</b> Portfolio + Risk <small>Targets and constraints</small></li><li><b>05</b> Japanese broker planning <small>Preview only; no order submission</small></li></ol><p>Diagram of the public architecture. Not a software screenshot.</p></div></div><section class="home-section"><p class="eyebrow">RESEARCH → PLAN → INSPECT</p><h2>One workflow. Several ways in.</h2><div class="feature-grid"><div><h3>Extend your research</h3><p>Register versioned factors and strategies with validators. Keep research contracts explicit and decisions inspectable.</p><a href="/docs/architecture/">Explore the architecture</a></div><div><h3>Simulate locally</h3><p>Separate research marks from execution quotes. Review historical backtests and local paper journals.</p><a href="/examples/offline-demo/">Run a synthetic example</a></div><div><h3>Use your interface</h3><p>Use shared services through Python, CLI, the desktop workbench or a workspace-bounded MCP agent.</p><a href="/docs/mcp/">Connect an MCP client</a></div></div></section><section class="demo-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">OFFLINE BY DESIGN</p><h2>Your first run needs no API key.</h2><p>The offline demo creates fictional inputs only. Real research requires data you select and are licensed to use; this site and package do not bundle J-Quants market history. The five multilingual GUI courses document the full local workflow.</p><a href="https://github.com/Siyuan-chat/KabuForge/blob/main/docs/en_US/GUI_RESEARCH_COURSES.md">Read the GUI research courses</a><a href="/docs/quickstart/">Follow the complete quickstart</a></div><div class="code"><button type="button" class="copy">Copy</button><pre><code>python -m pip install .
kabuforge doctor
kabuforge demo --out output/demo</code></pre><span class="copy-status" role="status"></span></div></section><section class="boundary"><h2>Know what the result establishes.</h2><p>All research is RESEARCH-ONLY with PIT guarantee false. TOPIX is a price-only reference without dividends. Explicit read-only broker diagnostics do not prove terminal connectivity; actual terminal access remains unverified. Real order submit and cancel are disabled, and the public Regime workflow is off by default.</p><a href="/docs/methodology/">Read the methodology and limitations</a></section></Layout>